1
00:00:04,571 --> 00:00:06,505
Come on, pay up your taxes!

2
00:00:06,573 --> 00:00:09,235
Guards, take this to the Sheriff.

3
00:00:11,311 --> 00:00:13,541
Taxes, we do not like.

4
00:00:15,782 --> 00:00:18,580
Phew! Well done, lads.

5
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,646
Hello, there.

6
00:00:27,527 --> 00:00:28,892
We're winning.

7
00:00:32,732 --> 00:00:34,427
Sorry, my lord.

8
00:00:34,501 --> 00:00:37,902
Come on, we are really winning.

9
00:00:37,971 --> 00:00:42,032
But there's one more prize
if we really want to beat the Sheriff.

10
00:00:57,824 --> 00:00:59,792
How do we know there is a strong room?

11
00:00:59,859 --> 00:01:02,623
- A wild guess.
- A little bird told him,

12
00:01:02,695 --> 00:01:05,027
a little Marian bird.

13
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:07,593
This is it.

14
00:01:12,272 --> 00:01:17,232
- Djaq.
- This? It's just a door.

15
00:01:17,310 --> 00:01:18,709
No handle, no lock.

16
00:01:22,248 --> 00:01:23,510
Robin!

17
00:01:25,051 --> 00:01:27,315
I do not like this!

18
00:01:27,387 --> 00:01:28,752
Will?

19
00:01:35,728 --> 00:01:38,288
- Will, what's this?
- Much, don't touch that!

20
00:01:41,468 --> 00:01:44,130
Why do I do it?

21
00:01:44,204 --> 00:01:46,434
- I'll check it out.
- Quick, quick!

22
00:01:46,506 --> 00:01:48,701
Turn it, turn it!

23
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:55,745
What is this?

24
00:01:55,815 --> 00:01:58,045
The Sheriff's war chest.

25
00:01:59,352 --> 00:02:01,286
And that is our poor chest, lads.

26
00:02:06,326 --> 00:02:09,352
- I'm not equipped for this.
- Robin, dogs!

27
00:02:09,429 --> 00:02:11,556
I know.

28
00:02:11,631 --> 00:02:12,825
But we'll be back.

29
00:02:55,074 --> 00:02:57,565
Am I to drown in everyone's incompetence

30
00:02:57,644 --> 00:03:00,772
whilst Robin Hood steals everything
that is rightfully mine?

31
00:03:00,847 --> 00:03:02,781
And clue - no!

32
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:05,613
Do something about it, Gisborne!

33
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:09,177
We know the strong room works.
It stopped Hood dead in his tracks.

34
00:03:09,255 --> 00:03:11,382
Not dead enough!

35
00:03:11,457 --> 00:03:14,585
Stealing the money from me
on the way here is one thing,

36
00:03:14,661 --> 00:03:17,528
stealing from right under my very nose
is another!

37
00:03:17,597 --> 00:03:20,794
The Black Knights are coming,
expecting their share-out.

38
00:03:20,867 --> 00:03:23,768
At this rate, there'll
be nothing left to share.

39
00:03:23,836 --> 00:03:28,796
I want Hood caught, Gisborne,
I want him dead.

40
00:03:30,977 --> 00:03:34,344
Meanwhile, how's your German?

41
00:03:34,414 --> 00:03:37,383
- German?
- Pat, woman, pat - don't rub.

42
00:03:38,785 --> 00:03:41,777
- Ah, this guest you're expecting.
- Yes.

43
00:03:41,854 --> 00:03:46,484
Count Friedrich of Bavaria is one of
the richest aristocrats in Europe.

44
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:49,592
And stupid, too, so...

45
00:03:49,662 --> 00:03:51,289
you and he should get on.

46
00:03:51,364 --> 00:03:53,730
He also has a weakness for gambling.

47
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:56,496
- Your alterations to the Great Hall.
- Yes.

48
00:03:56,569 --> 00:03:59,629
We will extend the Count
every courtesy, Gisborne -

49
00:03:59,706 --> 00:04:02,368
I've taken my bath six months early
for a reason.

50
00:04:02,442 --> 00:04:08,347
And then we shall take the in-bred booby
for every penny that he's got.

51
00:04:24,364 --> 00:04:27,629
The Sheriff wanted me to thank you all
for your hard work

52
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:30,168
building his new strong room.

53
00:04:30,236 --> 00:04:33,535
Slave labor, more like.
Where's our money?

54
00:04:35,241 --> 00:04:37,937
You'll get what's coming to you.

55
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:45,176
Now, how did Robin Hood find
out about the strong room?

56
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:50,612
Somebody must've told him.

57
00:04:53,793 --> 00:04:56,261
Loose talk costs lives.

58
00:05:05,605 --> 00:05:07,835
Good. Very good.

59
00:05:10,443 --> 00:05:12,934
This world is full of idiots,

60
00:05:13,012 --> 00:05:15,845
waiting to be parted from their money.

61
00:05:15,915 --> 00:05:17,815
But as you know...

62
00:05:19,819 --> 00:05:22,413
the house always wins.

63
00:05:23,823 --> 00:05:26,417
Now, I've had this table put here
in the middle

64
00:05:26,492 --> 00:05:29,017
because dice is
the Count's favorite game

65
00:05:29,095 --> 00:05:32,189
and this is the first thing he'll see
when he arrives.

66
00:05:33,399 --> 00:05:35,060
Good. Carry on.

67
00:05:37,136 --> 00:05:40,037
Ah! Lady Marian.

68
00:05:40,106 --> 00:05:41,437
There you are.

69
00:05:41,507 --> 00:05:45,443
Now, our guest is due to arrive very shortly

70
00:05:45,511 --> 00:05:49,572
and I'd like you to be a friend to him.

71
00:05:49,649 --> 00:05:53,107
I'd like you to make him feel
that his every desire...

72
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:54,813
is yours to obey.

73
00:05:54,887 --> 00:05:56,821
- Every desire?
- Mm.

74
00:05:57,990 --> 00:05:59,821
Show him a good time.

75
00:06:01,194 --> 00:06:03,662
- What do you think, Gisborne?
- Good idea.

76
00:06:03,730 --> 00:06:05,789
Huh! No, I won't.

77
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:08,060
Oh, yes, you will, missy.

78
00:06:09,302 --> 00:06:11,361
How's your father? So to speak.

79
00:06:11,437 --> 00:06:12,904
Frail.

80
00:06:12,972 --> 00:06:15,202
House arrest doesn't help.

81
00:06:15,274 --> 00:06:17,970
But very much alive.

82
00:06:22,014 --> 00:06:23,879
He'll see my heart isn't in it.

83
00:06:23,950 --> 00:06:27,181
Then pretend.
Deception comes easily enough to you.

84
00:06:27,253 --> 00:06:31,383
Now, when the Count arrives,
I want you to smile for him

85
00:06:31,457 --> 00:06:35,587
and buy yourself a gown that erm...
how shall I say?

86
00:06:35,661 --> 00:06:39,392
Stimulates the imagination.

87
00:06:39,465 --> 00:06:40,659
Uh-uh.

88
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:45,200
The cheaper the better, I think.

89
00:06:51,711 --> 00:06:52,837
Fetch.

90
00:07:01,053 --> 00:07:02,247
Stand further off.

91
00:07:03,389 --> 00:07:06,017
You make me feel as if I am under arrest.

92
00:07:08,461 --> 00:07:10,520
Trinkets for the lovely lady?

93
00:07:20,506 --> 00:07:23,873
You call this fresh? You can't expect
people to eat this muck.

94
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:30,514
Hey! Stop it!

95
00:07:30,583 --> 00:07:32,016
What you doing?

96
00:07:33,419 --> 00:07:36,946
- They have you well guarded.
- Why did I choose this?

97
00:07:37,023 --> 00:07:39,924
I can hardly breathe in there.

98
00:07:39,992 --> 00:07:42,756
- What happened?
- They're expecting a guest today,

99
00:07:42,829 --> 00:07:46,959
a rich German count, and they're
making me fawn over him, dress up...

100
00:07:47,033 --> 00:07:50,969
A German? Are the Sheriff and Prince John
looking for allies abroad?

101
00:07:51,037 --> 00:07:53,096
He's not an ally, he's a gambler.

102
00:07:53,172 --> 00:07:55,402
The Sheriff has set up gaming tables

103
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:59,104
and he plans to fill his strong room
with the Count's money.

104
00:07:59,178 --> 00:08:03,239
You see - another good reason to rob him.

105
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:05,841
Robin, do not go down there -
it's dangerous.

106
00:08:05,918 --> 00:08:07,613
Well, you know me -

107
00:08:07,687 --> 00:08:09,552
I like a challenge.

108
00:08:12,258 --> 00:08:14,818
- You don't have to do this.
- Yes, I do.

109
00:08:14,894 --> 00:08:17,795
Without me, you wouldn't know
about the strong room.

110
00:08:17,864 --> 00:08:21,391
- "England needs me. "
- Yes! England needs me.

111
00:08:21,467 --> 00:08:22,729
England needs us.

112
00:08:22,802 --> 00:08:24,929
And I need you.

113
00:08:29,475 --> 00:08:30,533
Guard!

114
00:08:32,178 --> 00:08:35,636
We need to break into the strong room
so I thought of Stephen.

115
00:08:35,715 --> 00:08:38,650
- Is he a friend of your father's?
- No, a teacher.

116
00:08:38,718 --> 00:08:42,415
A legend in his day. He doesn't work
any more but he used to be famous.

117
00:08:42,488 --> 00:08:47,425
He went to the Orient. They were his
apprentices Gisborne had killed today.

118
00:08:48,661 --> 00:08:50,128
Will.

119
00:08:52,598 --> 00:08:55,897
Still passionate, angry?

120
00:08:55,968 --> 00:08:58,528
- Lots to be angry about.
- True.

121
00:08:58,604 --> 00:09:02,199
And your skills - you're using them?

122
00:09:02,275 --> 00:09:03,799
Not wasting them?

123
00:09:03,876 --> 00:09:05,935
- I'm with Robin Hood.
- Good.

124
00:09:06,012 --> 00:09:07,707
That is not a waste.

125
00:09:11,484 --> 00:09:12,576
Do not touch that.

126
00:09:12,652 --> 00:09:13,880
Please.

127
00:09:13,953 --> 00:09:17,445
I have seen this type of work before.
It is Persian, no?

128
00:09:17,523 --> 00:09:19,388
It was my wife's.

129
00:09:22,962 --> 00:09:25,931
The men who died had families -
wives and children.

130
00:09:27,233 --> 00:09:30,600
- I want them to be taken care of.
- They will be.

131
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:32,934
You have my word.

132
00:09:33,005 --> 00:09:37,408
If there is any information you can give us,
anything that they told you.

133
00:09:37,476 --> 00:09:42,379
Look, I'm not being funny -
we've seen this death trap in action, right?

134
00:09:42,448 --> 00:09:44,348
And we're taking a blind man's advice?

135
00:09:48,054 --> 00:09:53,583
When a man loses his sight, he finds
compensation in the senses that remain.

136
00:10:00,499 --> 00:10:05,527
I do not intend on joining your mission
but I might be of assistance planning it.

137
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:08,768
But what do you know
about the Sheriff's strong room?

138
00:10:08,841 --> 00:10:11,537
A great deal.

139
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:13,169
I designed it.

140
00:10:51,117 --> 00:10:52,414
Marian!

141
00:10:52,485 --> 00:10:54,510
Who'd have thought?

142
00:10:54,587 --> 00:10:57,147
Ah! Count Friedrich.

143
00:10:57,223 --> 00:10:58,622
Welcome to Nottingham.

144
00:10:58,691 --> 00:11:01,660
Tell me, are all of the roads
in England so bad?

145
00:11:01,727 --> 00:11:06,528
- I feel like I have been beaten like the egg.
- Your safety was my first concern.

146
00:11:06,599 --> 00:11:09,762
I organized the route
so as to avoid the forest.

147
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:12,770
We couldn't have your fortune
or your good self

148
00:11:12,838 --> 00:11:14,601
falling into outlaws' hands.

149
00:11:14,674 --> 00:11:19,338
Myself and my men are a match
for any rustic ruffian, I assure you.

150
00:11:21,247 --> 00:11:23,442
Ah!

151
00:11:29,789 --> 00:11:33,623
Had I know what awaited me here,
I would've employed winged horses.

152
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:38,758
Er, Lady Marian has made it
her personal responsibility

153
00:11:38,831 --> 00:11:42,164
to make sure your stay is
as comfortable as possible.

154
00:11:43,202 --> 00:11:46,933
- Really?
- I'm happy to make your acquaintance.

155
00:11:47,006 --> 00:11:50,806
Oh, come, come. Acquaintances
are for old ladies and priests.

156
00:11:50,876 --> 00:11:53,470
We will dispense with such formalities.

157
00:11:54,046 --> 00:11:55,673
I am already your friend

158
00:11:55,748 --> 00:11:57,875
and always your servant.

159
00:12:00,052 --> 00:12:01,485
Oh, no!

160
00:12:02,288 --> 00:12:05,917
Do be careful, there!
Take the chest to my rooms!

161
00:12:09,628 --> 00:12:13,029
It's a few shillings for the gaming tables.

162
00:12:13,099 --> 00:12:15,932
Tell me, do you play, Lady Marian?

163
00:12:16,001 --> 00:12:18,663
Such pursuits are not entirely to my tastes.

164
00:12:18,738 --> 00:12:22,674
Then we must find pursuits
that excite you more.

165
00:12:22,742 --> 00:12:24,505
Tell me, do you ride?

166
00:12:30,616 --> 00:12:32,083
Come on, come on.

167
00:12:42,695 --> 00:12:44,458
Leaving so soon?

168
00:12:48,667 --> 00:12:51,568
Got your message.
What have you got for me?

169
00:12:54,807 --> 00:12:58,208
Robin wants to have another go
at your strong room.

170
00:12:58,277 --> 00:13:00,837
Obviously. And?

171
00:13:02,214 --> 00:13:06,173
Well, that's it. It'll be the next few days.
You'd better be ready.

172
00:13:06,252 --> 00:13:10,382
Don't waste my time!
I don't pay for obvious.

173
00:13:10,456 --> 00:13:12,424
You'll have to do better than that.

174
00:13:12,491 --> 00:13:14,152
Like what?

175
00:13:15,261 --> 00:13:17,661
Who told Robin Hood
about the strong room?

176
00:13:22,301 --> 00:13:23,359
Dunno.

177
00:13:24,270 --> 00:13:25,931
I don't, honest.

178
00:13:27,306 --> 00:13:31,970
It's early days in our relationship
but come to me again with nothing

179
00:13:32,044 --> 00:13:34,740
and I'll be very disappointed, understand?

180
00:13:34,814 --> 00:13:36,179
Yep.

181
00:13:36,248 --> 00:13:37,647
Got it.

182
00:13:40,119 --> 00:13:42,644
Don't make me wait too long.

183
00:13:51,630 --> 00:13:54,155
The designs were not meant
for the Sheriff.

184
00:13:54,233 --> 00:13:56,360
- They were a commission.
- For who?

185
00:13:56,435 --> 00:13:58,494
A Persian general.

186
00:13:58,571 --> 00:14:02,974
I did not complete the work
but I kept the plans with me always.

187
00:14:03,042 --> 00:14:06,375
Then not long ago,
my apprentice sold them to the Sheriff.

188
00:14:06,445 --> 00:14:09,243
His family were starving,
I can't blame him.

189
00:14:09,315 --> 00:14:10,782
He died for it.

190
00:14:10,850 --> 00:14:14,342
No expense has been spared
for your gambling pleasure.

191
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:17,150
Food, drink,

192
00:14:17,223 --> 00:14:18,554
company.

193
00:14:18,624 --> 00:14:21,957
We aim to please in every respect,
isn't that right, Marian?

194
00:14:24,063 --> 00:14:27,760
- Is this your idea of sport?
- You do not like the skittles?

195
00:14:27,833 --> 00:14:31,826
- But it is a charming game.
- A child's game, surely?

196
00:14:31,904 --> 00:14:35,704
- Hm!
- Do men really waste money on this?

197
00:14:35,774 --> 00:14:37,742
No waste if the prize is worth having.

198
00:14:38,844 --> 00:14:41,677
Come, let me show you.
Gently caress the ball...

199
00:14:43,115 --> 00:14:44,878
Danke schön. I thank you.

200
00:14:46,819 --> 00:14:48,150
Ow!

201
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:50,552
Forgive me - my aim was a little wide.

202
00:14:50,623 --> 00:14:52,352
Ja!

203
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:58,720
This is the door, the only entrance or exit
- there's no windows.

204
00:14:58,797 --> 00:15:01,766
The room itself is 20 feet long
by 20 feet wide,

205
00:15:01,834 --> 00:15:05,736
both walls are honeycombed with blow-holes,
each loaded with arrows

206
00:15:05,804 --> 00:15:07,897
primed to strike a specific spot.

207
00:15:07,973 --> 00:15:09,941
You step on the wrong stone and...

208
00:15:12,511 --> 00:15:15,639
- Which stones?
- My great innovation.

209
00:15:17,249 --> 00:15:19,376
It changes.

210
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:23,113
Well, that's not possible. Is it?

211
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:29,027
A weighted wheel beneath the floor
rotates regularly.

212
00:15:29,094 --> 00:15:34,157
Each turn defines a new route,
changing the order of the sprung stones.

213
00:15:35,501 --> 00:15:40,404
So... any stone can trigger a trap,
at any time?

214
00:15:40,472 --> 00:15:43,202
I did not say it would be easy.

215
00:15:44,310 --> 00:15:47,074
This, I do not like.

216
00:15:50,182 --> 00:15:53,549
Come, Lady Marian, bring me some luck.

217
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:55,985
- Where have you been?
- An errand.

218
00:15:56,055 --> 00:15:58,785
He's quite taken with her.
Encourage him.

219
00:15:58,857 --> 00:16:00,825
He'll lose quicker.

220
00:16:05,030 --> 00:16:08,659
Marian just needs a little coaxing.
It's her way.

221
00:16:08,734 --> 00:16:10,827
She says no when she means yes.

222
00:16:10,903 --> 00:16:12,234
Really?

223
00:16:12,304 --> 00:16:15,068
Then I shall relish the challenge.

224
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:21,211
Lady Marian, I cannot roll
unless you help me.

225
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:23,248
No, thank you.

226
00:16:23,315 --> 00:16:26,045
No, no, Lady Marian. I insist.

227
00:16:42,434 --> 00:16:44,493
- Lady Marian wins!
- You see?

228
00:16:44,570 --> 00:16:45,867
I win!

229
00:16:46,638 --> 00:16:49,630
Perhaps you will excuse me.
I have a headache.

230
00:16:49,708 --> 00:16:51,573
Oh, how terrible for you.

231
00:16:51,643 --> 00:16:56,808
If I may, I find that a gentle rubbing
of the temples is most effective.

232
00:16:56,882 --> 00:16:58,349
You are very kind.

233
00:16:58,417 --> 00:17:00,647
But I think I will go and lie down.

234
00:17:00,719 --> 00:17:03,688
As hard as it is, we must let you go.

235
00:17:03,756 --> 00:17:06,247
Thank you for your understanding, Count.

236
00:17:13,899 --> 00:17:15,423
Quite the beauty.

237
00:17:15,501 --> 00:17:18,197
I must confess,
when I first came to this country

238
00:17:18,270 --> 00:17:20,295
I thought I would not like it.

239
00:17:20,372 --> 00:17:23,535
But now, I like it very much!

240
00:17:31,683 --> 00:17:34,117
You'll be up against time.

241
00:17:34,186 --> 00:17:38,316
Opening the door turns an hourglass
set beside the base of the plinth.

242
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:41,985
When the sand runs through,
a final fail-safe is triggered.

243
00:17:42,828 --> 00:17:44,921
I shouldn't ask but what, exactly?

244
00:17:44,997 --> 00:17:49,661
There is a vault behind the back wall
containing a vat of molten lead.

245
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:52,636
It is kept at a constant heat
by the kitchen fires.

246
00:17:52,704 --> 00:17:56,640
When the hourglass is empty,
the vat is turned,

247
00:17:56,708 --> 00:17:59,700
the liquid flows into a series of gutters.

248
00:17:59,778 --> 00:18:01,973
The pipes in the walls!

249
00:18:02,047 --> 00:18:05,346
Burning liquid sprays out,
covering the entire room.

250
00:18:05,417 --> 00:18:07,578
Anyone inside will not stand a chance.

251
00:18:07,653 --> 00:18:13,250
And yet the coins remain intact because
they are harder than the soft lead.

252
00:18:14,660 --> 00:18:18,756
Well, all I'm hearing is arrows, lead,
and certain death.

253
00:18:18,831 --> 00:18:21,197
Encouraging.

254
00:18:22,301 --> 00:18:26,067
- How long does the hourglass take?
- A slow count of eight score and ten.

255
00:18:26,138 --> 00:18:30,973
In a count of 170, you've got to
get to the money and get it out.

256
00:18:31,043 --> 00:18:35,810
- Nice of you to join us, Allan.
- Well, I still think you're mad.

257
00:18:35,881 --> 00:18:38,577
- But if you want help...
- We are mad!

258
00:18:38,650 --> 00:18:41,676
We're just sick of robbing merchants
in the forest.

259
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:46,622
- That, we are good at.
- Then we'll work to get better at this.

260
00:18:48,293 --> 00:18:51,558
- We'll meet near the old barn, near Clun.
- What for?

261
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:56,397
To practice. We are going to build
this strong room over there.

262
00:18:58,437 --> 00:18:59,404
Good.

263
00:19:02,474 --> 00:19:05,102
Oh. Excuse me, can I pass?

264
00:19:05,177 --> 00:19:09,341
Orders. No one passes, not even you.
Sheriff's private room.

265
00:19:09,414 --> 00:19:11,143
Lady Marian?

266
00:19:11,216 --> 00:19:13,810
Oh, no. Let me pass just this once, please.

267
00:19:13,886 --> 00:19:17,822
What's in it for me?
Nice gown, very fetching.

268
00:19:17,890 --> 00:19:20,324
- Bit of a new look for you.
- How dare you!

269
00:19:20,392 --> 00:19:22,383
Just being friendly.

270
00:19:23,462 --> 00:19:25,259
How about a little kiss?

271
00:19:26,298 --> 00:19:29,290
How about a little smack?

272
00:19:29,368 --> 00:19:30,335
Excuse me.

273
00:19:33,205 --> 00:19:36,663
- You are an impressive fighter.
- Yes, I know.

274
00:19:36,742 --> 00:19:39,643
And you are also very impressive
in many ways.

275
00:19:39,711 --> 00:19:42,236
- Please.
- Are you not glad I came after you?

276
00:19:42,314 --> 00:19:46,375
- I made no invitation.
- You feign a headache and retire.

277
00:19:46,451 --> 00:19:50,148
I follow. This is the way that trysts
are made all over the world.

278
00:19:50,222 --> 00:19:53,055
Well, this one is all over, all right.

279
00:19:53,125 --> 00:19:54,615
As of now.

280
00:19:54,693 --> 00:19:57,856
- Gisborne!
- We mustn't be found here.

281
00:20:03,168 --> 00:20:04,533
Come, quick.

282
00:20:07,639 --> 00:20:10,301
There should be a guard on that door
at all times.

283
00:20:10,375 --> 00:20:13,242
- I'll look into immediately, my lord.
- Wait.

284
00:20:13,312 --> 00:20:16,839
First things first - tomorrow's meeting.
Come here.

285
00:20:21,987 --> 00:20:27,425
There. I have outlined the division
of the money in my strong room.

286
00:20:29,628 --> 00:20:35,396
You will be in charge of making sure our
friends the Black Knights get their share.

287
00:20:35,467 --> 00:20:39,403
You wish to strengthen our forces
in the south? The share is generous.

288
00:20:39,471 --> 00:20:42,440
Strategy, Gisborne.

289
00:20:43,041 --> 00:20:46,909
The King is most likely to land there
on his return.

290
00:20:46,979 --> 00:20:51,575
Besides, there will be plenty of funds
in the war chest

291
00:20:51,650 --> 00:20:54,744
after our German booby loses tonight.

292
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:57,721
And we'll make sure he loses big.

293
00:20:57,789 --> 00:21:01,520
- What if Count surprises us and wins?
- Wins?

294
00:21:01,593 --> 00:21:02,753
That buffoon?

295
00:21:02,828 --> 00:21:06,730
"Oh, I feel like I have beaten like ze egg. "

296
00:21:06,798 --> 00:21:08,425
Mincing oaf.

297
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:13,369
- But you have made provision?
- You know me too well, Gisborne.

298
00:21:13,438 --> 00:21:14,700
Of course.

299
00:21:14,773 --> 00:21:18,539
All eventualities have been considered.

300
00:21:19,878 --> 00:21:21,869
Dice that only roll one way -

301
00:21:22,981 --> 00:21:24,608
in our favor.

302
00:21:24,683 --> 00:21:27,151
Make sure Marian is with us tonight.

303
00:21:39,364 --> 00:21:43,266
What does he think?
That I will not be suspicious

304
00:21:43,368 --> 00:21:47,065
of an invitation out of the blue
from a Sheriff in... Where are we?

305
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:49,266
That I will not do some homework on him?

306
00:21:49,341 --> 00:21:53,141
Does he not think that his reputation
has not spread to Europe?

307
00:21:53,211 --> 00:21:55,236
And you - you are in on this little plan.

308
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:59,546
It's not the first time
I've been offered a girl to distract me.

309
00:21:59,618 --> 00:22:01,313
Let go of me!

310
00:22:01,386 --> 00:22:04,287
Do you people think
that I am a complete idiot?

311
00:22:04,356 --> 00:22:07,416
Yes - which is exactly
what you wanted, isn't it?

312
00:22:07,492 --> 00:22:10,052
- What do you mean?
- Oh, come on.

313
00:22:10,128 --> 00:22:13,723
The way you fight - you are no booby.

314
00:22:13,799 --> 00:22:16,529
I don't think a booby
does homework on his hosts.

315
00:22:16,601 --> 00:22:19,695
It suits you to have people
think you are an idiot.

316
00:22:19,771 --> 00:22:22,604
It helps, sometimes -
people play less cautiously

317
00:22:22,674 --> 00:22:23,971
but I am no cheat.

318
00:22:24,042 --> 00:22:27,978
And for what it's worth,
I am no lackey of the Sheriff.

319
00:22:28,046 --> 00:22:29,343
So...

320
00:22:29,414 --> 00:22:31,177
we are both players.

321
00:22:32,451 --> 00:22:35,249
- What will you do?
- Do? Leave.

322
00:22:35,320 --> 00:22:37,481
If the Sheriff is loading the dice,
I cannot win.

323
00:22:37,556 --> 00:22:40,184
I'll be struck by a sudden illness.

324
00:22:41,827 --> 00:22:44,591
Don't leave. Help me.

325
00:22:45,497 --> 00:22:48,432
- Help you.
- You heard the Sheriff.

326
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:51,298
He's using the money
to plot against the King.

327
00:22:51,370 --> 00:22:56,239
I have friends who want to relieve him
of his money before he distributes it

328
00:22:56,308 --> 00:22:58,799
and that'll have to be tonight.

329
00:22:58,877 --> 00:23:01,778
This is a dangerous game.

330
00:23:01,847 --> 00:23:03,337
But you're a player.

331
00:23:07,853 --> 00:23:10,947
The hourglass turns now.

332
00:23:11,022 --> 00:23:12,046
- One...
- Arrow!

333
00:23:12,157 --> 00:23:15,558
...two, three, four, five...

334
00:23:15,627 --> 00:23:17,390
- Oof!
- John, no!

335
00:23:17,462 --> 00:23:19,430
- Stone!
- Not there, John, no.

336
00:23:19,498 --> 00:23:21,159
- Then where?
- There!

337
00:23:21,233 --> 00:23:23,201
- Stone? He's pit.
- I'm pit!

338
00:23:23,268 --> 00:23:26,032
Stop it! Shut up!

339
00:23:28,707 --> 00:23:30,675
Lives depend on this.

340
00:23:32,210 --> 00:23:34,508
The wives and families of the dead.

341
00:23:34,579 --> 00:23:38,140
Not to mention what happens if the Sheriff
gives out that money.

342
00:23:40,452 --> 00:23:44,821
If we're going to defeat the strong room,
then we have to work as a team.

343
00:23:44,890 --> 00:23:47,154
And that means discipline.

344
00:23:49,661 --> 00:23:51,595
What do you think you're doing?

345
00:23:52,631 --> 00:23:56,032
- You stay in the castle.
- Believe me, I would rather stay here.

346
00:23:56,101 --> 00:23:58,228
I'm merely doing as I am instructed.

347
00:23:58,303 --> 00:24:01,568
Lady Marian is to ride out with me.

348
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:03,369
No. No.

349
00:24:03,442 --> 00:24:06,934
If I do not ride, I might be out of sorts

350
00:24:07,012 --> 00:24:10,573
and if I'm out of sorts,
I might not play the tables at all tonight.

351
00:24:12,451 --> 00:24:16,012
Very well.
I will provide you with an escort.

352
00:24:16,087 --> 00:24:19,215
Guards! The forest
is a very dangerous place.

353
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:21,885
Sheriff, we are both men of the world, ja?

354
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:25,123
Perhaps alone with nature,
out in the forest,

355
00:24:25,197 --> 00:24:28,530
Lady Marian might not
play so hard to get, hm?

356
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:30,261
No guards.

357
00:24:33,772 --> 00:24:35,364
Don't be late back.

358
00:24:46,117 --> 00:24:49,245
- There is a way, you know.
- A way to what?

359
00:24:50,355 --> 00:24:53,916
There is a way to do all the things
you need to do and still find love.

360
00:24:56,628 --> 00:25:00,394
You're a troubled soul. Be patient.

361
00:25:00,465 --> 00:25:02,194
You will prevail.

362
00:25:04,269 --> 00:25:07,432
And you can tell all that
by just feeling my face?

363
00:25:07,506 --> 00:25:10,942
No, your friend Much was telling me earlier.

364
00:25:15,013 --> 00:25:17,641
Now I am better acquainted
with your Sheriff,

365
00:25:17,716 --> 00:25:20,583
I understand your admiration for this outlaw.

366
00:25:20,652 --> 00:25:23,985
- It's not just me.
- I didn't mean just you.

367
00:25:24,055 --> 00:25:29,584
I think I would like to take to the woods
and fight injustice like your Robin Hood.

368
00:25:29,661 --> 00:25:30,992
What do you think?

369
00:25:31,062 --> 00:25:35,624
Why does a potential freedom fighter
waste his life gambling?

370
00:25:37,168 --> 00:25:38,601
I am a Count.

371
00:25:38,670 --> 00:25:41,867
My life has been managed
since the day that I was born.

372
00:25:41,973 --> 00:25:44,305
Tradition, etiquette -

373
00:25:44,376 --> 00:25:45,968
all so safe.

374
00:25:46,044 --> 00:25:48,706
I crave danger. You wouldn't understand.

375
00:25:49,714 --> 00:25:51,011
Don't be so sure.

376
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:04,828
You know how to find
these friends of yours?

377
00:26:04,896 --> 00:26:07,922
I'm hoping they're gonna find us.

378
00:26:07,999 --> 00:26:10,058
They already have.

379
00:26:18,710 --> 00:26:19,768
Who's your friend?

380
00:26:19,844 --> 00:26:22,904
Count Friedrich Bertrand Otto
von Wittersburg

381
00:26:22,981 --> 00:26:24,915
from the German duchy of Bavaria.

382
00:26:24,983 --> 00:26:26,951
And your friend.

383
00:26:30,455 --> 00:26:32,855
- This is the Sheriff's guest?
- Yes.

384
00:26:32,958 --> 00:26:36,587
- And you trust him to bring him here?
- He wants to help us.

385
00:26:36,661 --> 00:26:39,391
- Oh.
- It seems we have a common desire.

386
00:26:42,300 --> 00:26:45,633
We both wish to see
the Sheriff broken and humiliated.

387
00:26:45,704 --> 00:26:48,468
- Marian and I...
- First-name terms.

388
00:26:48,540 --> 00:26:50,838
- Jealous?
- Of him?

389
00:26:52,510 --> 00:26:54,137
Marian has a proposition.

390
00:26:54,212 --> 00:26:57,010
Robbing the strong room -
it has to be tonight.

391
00:26:57,082 --> 00:27:00,381
- Not possible, we're not ready.
- Then don't bother at all.

392
00:27:00,452 --> 00:27:04,548
The Sheriff will divide the money between
the Black Knights tomorrow.

393
00:27:04,623 --> 00:27:07,319
After that, the strong room will be empty.

394
00:27:09,461 --> 00:27:12,396
I don't like that look.
That look means trouble.

395
00:27:12,464 --> 00:27:14,932
Robin, it's certain death.

396
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:19,266
Well, if that money's going to finance
weapons and men to kill the King,

397
00:27:19,337 --> 00:27:21,396
then we're dead already.

398
00:27:35,654 --> 00:27:37,349
- Kiss me.
- What?

399
00:27:37,422 --> 00:27:40,858
Otherwise what will they think
we've been doing all this time?

400
00:27:41,359 --> 00:27:43,224
Oh!

401
00:27:43,294 --> 00:27:45,091
Ahhh!

402
00:27:45,163 --> 00:27:48,894
- We have a budding romance after all.
- So it would seem.

403
00:27:48,967 --> 00:27:52,368
Hmm. Maybe one more?
To make it really convincing?

404
00:27:52,437 --> 00:27:54,064
Careful.

405
00:27:54,172 --> 00:27:57,164
- Remember the skittles.
- Ah, ja.

406
00:27:57,242 --> 00:28:00,609
He succeeded where you failed, Gisborne.

407
00:28:00,679 --> 00:28:04,240
Come along, money to be made.

408
00:28:17,095 --> 00:28:18,995
You - stop.

409
00:28:25,170 --> 00:28:29,937
I want the Count's goblet filled
at all times tonight, do you understand?

410
00:28:30,008 --> 00:28:31,737
Go on.

411
00:28:39,818 --> 00:28:41,809
You know what to do.

412
00:28:43,054 --> 00:28:46,785
There - the money you lose tonight
goes into that.

413
00:28:46,858 --> 00:28:49,292
It connects directly
to the strong room below.

414
00:28:49,360 --> 00:28:51,954
- Now, once it's in there...
- Ja, ja, I know.

415
00:28:52,030 --> 00:28:55,727
Our outlaw friends will steal
it back for me. It seems unfair.

416
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:59,201
- I don't like to lose, even on purpose.
- Well, if you win,

417
00:28:59,270 --> 00:29:02,137
the Sheriff won't let you
leave Nottingham alive.

418
00:29:02,841 --> 00:29:06,140
I was running towards the Great Hall
and I tripped and fell

419
00:29:06,211 --> 00:29:09,738
and I think I've hurt my ankle - look!

420
00:29:13,551 --> 00:29:15,746
Men are so obvious.

421
00:29:15,820 --> 00:29:20,382
Now, play as long as you can.
Take your time.

422
00:29:20,458 --> 00:29:25,020
And then, when we get the signal...
start losing.

423
00:29:40,612 --> 00:29:43,080
Oh, didn't recognize you.

424
00:29:52,056 --> 00:29:54,217
- What?
- Nothing.

425
00:29:57,695 --> 00:30:00,721
- You wanna dress like a girl more often.
- Oh, I do, do I?

426
00:30:00,799 --> 00:30:02,061
It's just a thought.

427
00:30:08,173 --> 00:30:10,573
- Count Friedrich.
- Ah!

428
00:30:10,642 --> 00:30:11,836
Fortune awaits - good luck.

429
00:30:13,711 --> 00:30:17,704
Lady Marian is my good luck charm
for this evening.

430
00:30:17,782 --> 00:30:21,047
You know, Gisborne, I have
a new-found respect for our Marian.

431
00:30:21,152 --> 00:30:24,349
Are we to endure this ritual
at every turn?

432
00:30:24,422 --> 00:30:29,951
Let him lose in his own way.
And if he doesn't... we'll switch the dice.

433
00:30:30,028 --> 00:30:32,690
- Oh!
- Ah!

434
00:30:32,764 --> 00:30:35,426
- I won.
- Throw.

435
00:30:37,202 --> 00:30:38,829
Count Friedrich wins!

436
00:30:43,374 --> 00:30:44,864
The Count wins!

437
00:30:47,979 --> 00:30:50,277
The Count wins!

438
00:30:57,255 --> 00:30:59,052
- Again!
- I win!

439
00:31:05,363 --> 00:31:07,558
No dogs this time.

440
00:31:17,475 --> 00:31:20,672
- Where's the arrow?
- I don't know.

441
00:31:21,779 --> 00:31:24,043
Go on, Will.

442
00:31:29,053 --> 00:31:30,577
Oh!

443
00:31:40,698 --> 00:31:42,529
Poison.

444
00:31:42,600 --> 00:31:44,158
That wasn't there before.

445
00:31:45,904 --> 00:31:48,395
They've changed the sequence.

446
00:31:48,473 --> 00:31:50,941
- Then we can't go on.
- It's our only chance.

447
00:31:51,009 --> 00:31:53,409
Our practicing is for nothing.

448
00:31:53,478 --> 00:31:57,039
If we do not try, then England will be lost.

449
00:31:57,115 --> 00:32:00,050
And if we're dead,
then that's my England lost.

450
00:32:05,390 --> 00:32:07,221
We go.

451
00:32:12,964 --> 00:32:14,591
All right.

452
00:32:15,667 --> 00:32:17,760
If we die, don't come running to me.

453
00:32:18,636 --> 00:32:20,604
Go on, Will.

454
00:32:20,672 --> 00:32:22,071
John?

455
00:32:32,350 --> 00:32:33,647
Ready?

456
00:32:38,056 --> 00:32:40,354
Djaq, tell Marian we're in.

457
00:32:40,425 --> 00:32:42,188
Allan, John, keep watch.

458
00:32:45,163 --> 00:32:47,188
Much.

459
00:32:53,404 --> 00:32:56,066
Do not take your eyes off that hourglass.

460
00:32:57,308 --> 00:32:58,434
Bow.

461
00:33:05,016 --> 00:33:06,210
They're in.

462
00:33:06,284 --> 00:33:08,218
Better start losing.

463
00:33:09,954 --> 00:33:14,516
If that's the way he loses, you may need
your contingency plan sooner than expected.

464
00:33:14,592 --> 00:33:17,755
We're about even. It's early yet.

465
00:33:33,311 --> 00:33:36,144
- Don't think about them.
- Marian.

466
00:33:36,214 --> 00:33:40,241
- We have to start losing... Time is running out.
- I'm doing my best.

467
00:33:48,292 --> 00:33:50,658
Go on!

468
00:33:57,702 --> 00:33:58,828
Watch out!

469
00:34:03,975 --> 00:34:06,773
Sheriff, let us make things interesting.

470
00:34:06,844 --> 00:34:12,373
Everything I have against
the entire contents of your strong room.

471
00:34:15,286 --> 00:34:17,811
As we say in Bavaria,

472
00:34:17,889 --> 00:34:21,381
Das letzte Hemd hat keine Taschen.

473
00:34:24,996 --> 00:34:27,226
You cannot take it with you.

474
00:34:28,399 --> 00:34:30,424
Sheriff, what do you say?

475
00:34:30,501 --> 00:34:32,264
It's only money.

476
00:34:37,842 --> 00:34:40,436
I agree.

477
00:34:59,897 --> 00:35:02,832
It's such a momentous game,

478
00:35:02,900 --> 00:35:07,735
might I suggest a change of dice?

479
00:35:08,439 --> 00:35:10,999
As you wish.

480
00:35:17,081 --> 00:35:18,173
Ja.

481
00:35:18,249 --> 00:35:19,978
I see.

482
00:35:22,553 --> 00:35:24,020
Uh-huh.

483
00:35:24,088 --> 00:35:26,113
Ja.

484
00:35:27,592 --> 00:35:31,619
You see? It's easy once you know how.

485
00:35:36,767 --> 00:35:38,394
Excellent.

486
00:35:42,573 --> 00:35:44,803
For luck.

487
00:35:44,876 --> 00:35:46,867
Ha-ha!

488
00:35:51,048 --> 00:35:53,539
The house wins!

489
00:35:58,022 --> 00:36:00,513
Hang on. What's this?

490
00:36:00,591 --> 00:36:04,118
- Master, get out of there. There's no time.
- Oh, Sheriff.

491
00:36:05,963 --> 00:36:07,396
It's another trick.

492
00:36:07,465 --> 00:36:12,596
It's an illusion, an image
thrown onto a sheet of glass.

493
00:36:20,111 --> 00:36:21,806
The money is not here.

494
00:36:23,648 --> 00:36:28,585
Lady Marian, you have brought me
nothing but back luck.

495
00:36:28,653 --> 00:36:31,019
Your attentions are no longer welcome.

496
00:36:31,088 --> 00:36:32,521
Auf wiedersehen.

497
00:36:38,229 --> 00:36:40,527
Well done, Marian.

498
00:36:40,598 --> 00:36:42,759
Wasn't so hard, was it?

499
00:36:42,833 --> 00:36:44,926
No. It wasn't.

500
00:36:48,239 --> 00:36:51,970
Excellent. The war chest
has doubled in one night.

501
00:36:54,045 --> 00:36:55,945
- Master, get out of there.
- Shh!

502
00:37:15,166 --> 00:37:16,724
Yeah.

503
00:37:16,801 --> 00:37:19,998
- What are you doing? Just leave it.
- We've come this far...

504
00:37:24,508 --> 00:37:26,976
- What's he doing?
- Wait!

505
00:37:31,048 --> 00:37:33,778
The money is here. The bags - quickly!

506
00:37:39,557 --> 00:37:41,787
Go on, Much. Give me those!

507
00:37:41,859 --> 00:37:43,622
All right, all right!

508
00:37:54,305 --> 00:37:57,604
- Marian!
- My men have the coach ready.

509
00:37:57,675 --> 00:38:00,735
- Your friends?
- If they have succeeded, we'll know soon.

510
00:38:00,811 --> 00:38:02,244
And if they haven't?

511
00:38:09,587 --> 00:38:10,918
Look, Master!

512
00:38:13,090 --> 00:38:14,284
Why...

513
00:38:14,358 --> 00:38:15,518
do we leave...

514
00:38:15,593 --> 00:38:19,359
everything to the last second?

515
00:38:19,430 --> 00:38:23,196
Well, I find it's more fun that way.

516
00:38:27,471 --> 00:38:28,460
No.

517
00:38:29,674 --> 00:38:31,232
Come on, let's go.

518
00:38:40,284 --> 00:38:42,582
The strong room?

519
00:38:42,653 --> 00:38:44,348
Guards!

520
00:38:44,422 --> 00:38:47,414
Help, you men, quickly -
the Sheriff is under attack.

521
00:39:16,287 --> 00:39:17,948
Look at you!

522
00:39:19,056 --> 00:39:22,150
Be careful. If I can see your friendship,
so may others.

523
00:39:22,226 --> 00:39:24,023
Don't worry. I crave the danger.

524
00:39:24,095 --> 00:39:27,895
If you are ever in Bavaria,
I remain, my lady, your servant,

525
00:39:27,965 --> 00:39:30,195
your booby and your friend.

526
00:39:32,069 --> 00:39:33,331
You're funny.

527
00:39:33,404 --> 00:39:36,066
- You are beautiful.
- You are leaving.

528
00:39:50,454 --> 00:39:54,151
My war chest - and the booby's money.

529
00:39:54,225 --> 00:39:57,353
But they can't have done! No! No!

530
00:39:59,363 --> 00:40:00,694
No!

531
00:40:00,765 --> 00:40:03,029
No! No!

532
00:40:03,100 --> 00:40:04,328
No!

533
00:40:05,369 --> 00:40:06,996
No!

534
00:40:18,482 --> 00:40:22,851
Count Friedrich will take you to the coast.
I cannot thank you enough for your help.

535
00:40:22,953 --> 00:40:27,117
Yes, you can.
The families of the men that died...

536
00:40:27,191 --> 00:40:28,954
We'll look after them.

537
00:40:30,761 --> 00:40:32,285
You will prevail.

538
00:40:39,403 --> 00:40:41,598
Now, you're sure about your route?

539
00:40:41,672 --> 00:40:44,937
Stick to the smaller roads.
The Sheriff will have the main ones covered.

540
00:40:45,009 --> 00:40:48,001
Ah, another bumpy ride. This country!

541
00:40:48,078 --> 00:40:50,876
By the time I get home,
I will be scrambled.

542
00:40:52,016 --> 00:40:53,540
Is this your money?

543
00:40:53,617 --> 00:40:55,778
Thank you, England is forever in your debt.

544
00:40:56,687 --> 00:40:58,416
Take it - keep it.

545
00:40:58,489 --> 00:41:01,856
- What?
- England's debt is to Lady Marian,

546
00:41:01,926 --> 00:41:03,325
not me.

547
00:41:03,394 --> 00:41:05,760
Spend it wisely, Robin Hood.

548
00:41:06,964 --> 00:41:08,363
About Marian...

549
00:41:08,432 --> 00:41:12,095
One gamble I would have
given anything to win.

550
00:41:12,169 --> 00:41:14,296
You are a lucky man, Robin Hood.

551
00:41:19,710 --> 00:41:21,177
Farewell.

552
00:41:27,384 --> 00:41:28,544
Right.

553
00:41:29,420 --> 00:41:30,819
Work to do.

554
00:41:36,961 --> 00:41:39,987
I'm not being funny
but the poor have it easy.

555
00:41:40,064 --> 00:41:42,624
I don't think so, Allan.

556
00:41:45,569 --> 00:41:47,469
This is what we do, lads.

557
00:41:47,571 --> 00:41:50,438
We've turned war chest into poor chest.

558
00:41:52,176 --> 00:41:55,509
Well, come on - we have
four more villages before sundown.

559
00:41:59,850 --> 00:42:02,819
I've been thinking -
we've never been to Germany.

560
00:42:02,887 --> 00:42:05,253
- No.
- If things don't work out here,

561
00:42:05,356 --> 00:42:08,154
then... maybe the Count'd have us over there.

562
00:42:08,225 --> 00:42:11,524
Mm. Much - Count of Schleswig Holstein.

563
00:42:12,663 --> 00:42:13,823
What's so funny?

564
00:42:14,465 --> 00:42:17,901
I can be Count of Shlessy or...
whatever.

565
00:42:17,968 --> 00:42:20,698
You can't be count of a place
you can't pronounce.

566
00:42:20,771 --> 00:42:24,969
- Not necessarily.
- Sovereign of Sherwood, mate, that's you.

567
00:42:25,042 --> 00:42:28,170
Well, that's us, lads.
Sovereigns of Sherwood.

